{{also|Lohikäärme}}
==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|l|o}}

===Etymology===
One of the many words made up by Michael Agricola during the Finnish translation of the New Testament. Compound of ''[[lohi]]'' and ''[[käärme]]'', can be translated as 'salmon snake'.

===Noun===
{{fi-noun|lohikäärme|type=sähke}}

# A [[dragon]]
# A [[wyvern]]

====Usage notes====
Most Finns don't make a difference between a "wyvern" (''[[traakki]]'') and "dragon" ('''''lohikäärme'''''), and would use ''lohikäärme'' to refer to both.

